        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">African socialism</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1956 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Thinkers</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-nyerere">Julius Nyerere</a> of Tanzania, author of Ujamaa; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwame-nkrumah">Kwame Nkrumah</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a>, whose philosophy is called Nkrumahism; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leopold-sedar-senghor">Léopold Sédar Senghor</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a>, poet of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/negritude">Négritude</a> movement; Abdoulaye Ly, whose 1956 book was the first influential socialist text tailored for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmed-sekou-toure">Sékou Touré</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea">Guinea</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modibo-keita">Modibo Keïta</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nelson-mandela">Nelson Mandela</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/desmond-tutu">Desmond Tutu</a>, who echoed its themes</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Key texts</span><span class="info-stat-val">Abdoulaye Ly's Les masses africaines et l'actuelle condition humaine (1956); the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arusha-declaration">Arusha Declaration</a> (1967); Nkrumah's A declaration to the colonial peoples; Senghor's The Challenge of Culture in French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a> and Vues sur l'Afrique noire, ou s'assimiler, non être assimilés; William H. Friedland and Carl G. Rosberg Jr., eds., African <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/socialism">Socialism</a></span></div>
